{"beat": 12, "name": "THE SOAP AND THE SKIMMER", "text": "Look at what that does to a buyer's mind. The soap barely pays. The skimmer pays handsomely. In a store with one price, the customer doesn't know which is which, and doesn't care. The store has to. So a one-price store isn't simple. It's simple on the outside, and on the inside it's a portfolio: every item carrying a different margin under the same tag, and the buyer's whole job is to keep the average above the line. That's the first thing Woolworth understood. Same tag, different margins. Which means, as we'll see, different best prices.", "provider": "placeholder", "words": [{"word": "Look", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.2}, {"word": "at", "start": 0.2, "end": 0.32}, {"word": "what", "start": 0.32, "end": 0.44}, {"word": "that", "start": 0.44, "end": 0.66}, {"word": "does", "start": 0.66, "end": 0.96}, {"word": "to", "start": 0.96, "end": 1.14}, {"word": "a", "start": 1.14, "end": 1.3}, {"word": "buyer's", "start": 1.3, "end": 1.76}, {"word": "mind.", "start": 1.76, "end": 2.08}, {"word": "The", "start": 2.64, "end": 2.76}, {"word": "soap", "start": 2.76, "end": 3.06}, {"word": "barely", "start": 3.06, "end": 3.42}, {"word": "pays.", "start": 3.42, "end": 3.84}, {"word": "The", "start": 4.44, "end": 4.62}, {"word": "skimmer", "start": 4.62, "end": 4.92}, {"word": "pays", "start": 4.92, "end": 5.34}, {"word": "handsomely.", "start": 5.34, "end": 6.02}, {"word": "In", "start": 6.54, "end": 6.64}, {"word": "a", "start": 6.64, "end": 6.76}, {"word": "store", "start": 6.76, "end": 7.04}, {"word": "with", "start": 7.04, "end": 7.3}, {"word": "one", "start": 7.3, "end": 7.52}, {"word": "price,", "start": 7.52, "end": 7.96}, {"word": "the", "start": 8.14, "end": 8.18}, {"word": "customer", "start": 8.18, "end": 8.58}, {"word": "doesn't", "start": 8.58, "end": 9.0}, {"word": "know", "start": 9.0, "end": 9.18}, {"word": "which", "start": 9.18, "end": 9.42}, {"word": "is", "start": 9.42, "end": 9.58}, {"word": "which,", "sta